{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Supervised Classification Benchmark on Iris Dataset\n",
    "## Logistic Regression vs. Decision Tree Classifier\n",
    "\n",
    "### Project Overview & Objectives\n",
    "This notebook demonstrates an end-to-end supervised machine learning classification pipeline:\n",
    "1. **Data Ingestion & Exploration:** Load benchmark dataset using Pandas and inspect summary statistics.\n",
    "2. **Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA):** Visualize feature distributions and class separation with Seaborn pairplots.\n",
    "3. **Data Preprocessing:** Split dataset into training and test sets (80/20 ratio) and normalize features using `StandardScaler`.\n",
    "4. **Model Training:** Train both a linear model (`LogisticRegression`) and a non-linear tree model (`DecisionTreeClassifier`).\n",
    "5. **Benchmarking & Evaluation:** Measure and compare Accuracy, Precision, Recall, and F1-score.\n",
    "6. **Visual Analysis:** Plot confusion matrix heatmaps, 2D decision boundary surfaces, and decision tree structures."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 1: Import Required Libraries"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "from sklearn.datasets import load_iris\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n",
    "from sklearn.tree import DecisionTreeClassifier, plot_tree\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import (\n",
    "    accuracy_score,\n",
    "    precision_score,\n",
    "    recall_score,\n",
    "    f1_score,\n",
    "    classification_report,\n",
    "    confusion_matrix\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Visual styling configuration\n",
    "sns.set_theme(style=\"whitegrid\", font_scale=1.1)\n",
    "plt.rcParams[\"figure.figsize\"] = (10, 6)\n",
    "print(\"Required libraries successfully imported.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 2: Load the Benchmark Dataset\n",
    "We load the Iris dataset into a Pandas DataFrame. A multi-source loader is implemented to prioritize the direct CSV URL while providing automated fallback to Scikit-Learn if offline."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "csv_url = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mwaskom/seaborn-data/master/iris.csv\"\n",
    "\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    # Attempt loading from URL\n",
    "    df = pd.read_csv(csv_url)\n",
    "    print(\"Loaded dataset successfully from URL.\")\n",
    "except Exception as e:\n",
    "    print(f\"Network load notice ({e}). Loading dataset from Scikit-Learn fallback...\")\n",
    "    raw_data = load_iris(as_frame=True)\n",
    "    df = raw_data.frame\n",
    "    df.columns = [\"sepal_length\", \"sepal_width\", \"petal_length\", \"petal_width\", \"species\"]\n",
    "    target_names = {0: \"setosa\", 1: \"versicolor\", 2: \"virginica\"}\n",
    "    if df[\"species\"].dtype != object:\n",
    "        df[\"species\"] = df[\"species\"].map(target_names)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Display dataset overview\n",
    "print(f\"Dataset shape: {df.shape[0]} rows, {df.shape[1]} columns\")\n",
    "display(df.head())\n",
    "display(df.info())\n",
    "print(\"\\nClass Distribution:\")\n",
    "print(df[\"species\"].value_counts())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 3: Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)\n",
    "Examining feature distributions, inter-feature correlations, and pairwise class separability."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Descriptive summary statistics for numerical features\n",
    "display(df.describe().T)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Check for any missing values\n",
    "print(\"Missing values per column:\")\n",
    "print(df.isnull().sum())\n",
    "\n",
    "# Pairplot using Seaborn to visualize feature interactions\n",
    "pairplot_fig = sns.pairplot(df, hue=\"species\", markers=[\"o\", \"s\", \"D\"], palette=\"viridis\", diag_kind=\"kde\")\n",
    "pairplot_fig.fig.suptitle(\"Pairwise Relationships across Iris Species\", y=1.02, fontsize=16)\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Feature correlation heatmap\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 6))\n",
    "feature_cols = [\"sepal_length\", \"sepal_width\", \"petal_length\", \"petal_width\"]\n",
    "corr = df[feature_cols].corr()\n",
    "sns.heatmap(corr, annot=True, cmap=\"coolwarm\", fmt=\".2f\", square=True, linewidths=0.5)\n",
    "plt.title(\"Feature Correlation Heatmap\", fontsize=14, pad=12)\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 4: Dataset Splitting & Feature Scaling\n",
    "- **Feature Matrix ($X$) & Target Vector ($y$):** Extract the four measurements as inputs and `species` as output labels.\n",
    "- **Train/Test Split (80/20):** Divide the data using stratified sampling to preserve proportional class balances.\n",
    "- **StandardScaler:** Normalize feature distributions so that each feature has zero mean ($\mu = 0$) and unit variance ($\sigma = 1$). To prevent data leakage, the scaler is fit **only** on the training partition."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X = df[feature_cols].values\n",
    "y = df[\"species\"].values\n",
    "\n",
    "# 80% training / 20% testing split with stratification\n",
    "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n",
    "    X,\n",
    "    y,\n",
    "    test_size=0.20,\n",
    "    random_state=42,\n",
    "    stratify=y\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Training samples: {X_train.shape[0]} | Testing samples: {X_test.shape[0]}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Initialize and apply StandardScaler\n",
    "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
    "X_train_scaled = scaler.fit_transform(X_train)\n",
    "X_test_scaled = scaler.transform(X_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Verify scaling properties on training set (Mean ~ 0, Std ~ 1)\n",
    "scaled_summary = pd.DataFrame(X_train_scaled, columns=feature_cols).agg([\"mean\", \"std\"]).round(4)\n",
    "print(\"\\nVerification of Scaled Training Data Distribution:\")\n",
    "display(scaled_summary)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 5: Supervised Model Training\n",
    "We train two distinct classification architectures:\n",
    "1. **Logistic Regression:** Linear classifier applying multinomial softmax modeling.\n",
    "2. **Decision Tree Classifier:** Non-linear rule-based tree partitioner."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 1. Initialize and train Logistic Regression\n",
    "log_reg = LogisticRegression(max_iter=200, random_state=42)\n",
    "log_reg.fit(X_train_scaled, y_train)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Initialize and train Decision Tree Classifier\n",
    "decision_tree = DecisionTreeClassifier(max_depth=3, random_state=42)\n",
    "decision_tree.fit(X_train_scaled, y_train)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Both Logistic Regression and Decision Tree models successfully trained.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 6: Benchmarking & Performance Metrics\n",
    "We evaluate model predictions on the held-out test partition across standard classification metrics:\n",
    "- **Accuracy:** Overall proportion of correct classifications.\n",
    "- **Precision (Macro & Weighted):** Ability to avoid false positive label assignments.\n",
    "- **Recall (Macro & Weighted):** Ability to correctly retrieve all ground truth instances.\n",
    "- **F1-Score (Macro & Weighted):** Harmonic mean balancing precision and recall."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Generate predictions\n",
    "y_pred_lr = log_reg.predict(X_test_scaled)\n",
    "y_pred_dt = decision_tree.predict(X_test_scaled)\n",
    "\n",
    "def calculate_metrics(y_true, y_pred):\n",
    "    return {\n",
    "        \"Accuracy\": accuracy_score(y_true, y_pred),\n",
    "        \"Precision (Macro)\": precision_score(y_true, y_pred, average=\"macro\"),\n",
    "        \"Precision (Weighted)\": precision_score(y_true, y_pred, average=\"weighted\"),\n",
    "        \"Recall (Macro)\": recall_score(y_true, y_pred, average=\"macro\"),\n",
    "        \"Recall (Weighted)\": recall_score(y_true, y_pred, average=\"weighted\"),\n",
    "        \"F1-Score (Macro)\": f1_score(y_true, y_pred, average=\"macro\"),\n",
    "        \"F1-Score (Weighted)\": f1_score(y_true, y_pred, average=\"weighted\")\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "metrics_lr = calculate_metrics(y_test, y_pred_lr)\n",
    "metrics_dt = calculate_metrics(y_test, y_pred_dt)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create comparative benchmark table\n",
    "benchmark_df = pd.DataFrame([metrics_lr, metrics_dt], index=[\"Logistic Regression\", \"Decision Tree\"]).round(4)\n",
    "print(\"\\n--- Model Performance Benchmark Table ---\")\n",
    "display(benchmark_df)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n--- Logistic Regression Classification Report ---\")\n",
    "print(classification_report(y_test, y_pred_lr))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"--- Decision Tree Classification Report ---\")\n",
    "print(classification_report(y_test, y_pred_dt))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 7: Confusion Matrix Heatmaps\n",
    "Visualize predicted vs actual class frequencies to inspect error patterns."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "labels = np.unique(y)\n",
    "cm_lr = confusion_matrix(y_test, y_pred_lr, labels=labels)\n",
    "cm_dt = confusion_matrix(y_test, y_pred_dt, labels=labels)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 5))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Logistic Regression Confusion Matrix\n",
    "sns.heatmap(cm_lr, annot=True, fmt=\"d\", cmap=\"Blues\", xticklabels=labels, yticklabels=labels, ax=axes[0])\n",
    "axes[0].set_title(f\"Logistic Regression (Acc: {metrics_lr['Accuracy']:.2f})\", fontsize=13)\n",
    "axes[0].set_xlabel(\"Predicted Label\")\n",
    "axes[0].set_ylabel(\"True Label\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Decision Tree Confusion Matrix\n",
    "sns.heatmap(cm_dt, annot=True, fmt=\"d\", cmap=\"Greens\", xticklabels=labels, yticklabels=labels, ax=axes[1])\n",
    "axes[1].set_title(f\"Decision Tree (Acc: {metrics_dt['Accuracy']:.2f})\", fontsize=13)\n",
    "axes[1].set_xlabel(\"Predicted Label\")\n",
    "axes[1].set_ylabel(\"True Label\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 8: Decision Boundary Visualization\n",
    "To visualize the spatial classification behavior of both models in 2D space, we train models on the two most discriminative features: `petal_length` and `petal_width`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Select 2 key features for intuitive 2D boundary visualization\n",
    "feat_indices = [2, 3]  # petal_length, petal_width\n",
    "feat_names = [feature_cols[i] for i in feat_indices]\n",
    "\n",
    "X_2d_train = X_train[:, feat_indices]\n",
    "X_2d_test = X_test[:, feat_indices]\n",
    "\n",
    "scaler_2d = StandardScaler()\n",
    "X_2d_train_sc = scaler_2d.fit_transform(X_2d_train)\n",
    "X_2d_test_sc = scaler_2d.transform(X_2d_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Encode string species labels into integers for boundary contour mapping\n",
    "species_map = {name: idx for idx, name in enumerate(labels)}\n",
    "y_train_num = np.array([species_map[s] for s in y_train])\n",
    "y_test_num = np.array([species_map[s] for s in y_test])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Retrain 2D models\n",
    "lr_2d = LogisticRegression(max_iter=200, random_state=42).fit(X_2d_train_sc, y_train_num)\n",
    "dt_2d = DecisionTreeClassifier(max_depth=3, random_state=42).fit(X_2d_train_sc, y_train_num)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create dense coordinate grid\n",
    "x_min, x_max = X_2d_train_sc[:, 0].min() - 1, X_2d_train_sc[:, 0].max() + 1\n",
    "y_min, y_max = X_2d_train_sc[:, 1].min() - 1, X_2d_train_sc[:, 1].max() + 1\n",
    "xx, yy = np.meshgrid(np.linspace(x_min, x_max, 300), np.linspace(y_min, y_max, 300))\n",
    "grid_pts = np.c_[xx.ravel(), yy.ravel()]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot decision surfaces side-by-side\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(15, 6))\n",
    "models_2d = [(\"Logistic Regression Decision Boundary\", lr_2d, axes[0]),\n",
    "             (\"Decision Tree Decision Boundary\", dt_2d, axes[1])]\n",
    "\n",
    "from matplotlib.colors import ListedColormap\n",
    "cmap_light = ListedColormap([\"#E6F0FA\", \"#FFF2E0\", \"#E8F5E9\"])\n",
    "cmap_bold = [\"#1f77b4\", \"#ff7f0e\", \"#2ca02c\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "for title, model, ax in models_2d:\n",
    "    Z = model.predict(grid_pts).reshape(xx.shape)\n",
    "    ax.contourf(xx, yy, Z, alpha=0.6, cmap=cmap_light)\n",
    "    ax.contour(xx, yy, Z, colors=\"gray\", linewidths=0.7, linestyles=\"--\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Scatter plot ground-truth points\n",
    "    for class_idx, class_name in enumerate(labels):\n",
    "        mask = (y_train_num == class_idx)\n",
    "        ax.scatter(X_2d_train_sc[mask, 0], X_2d_train_sc[mask, 1],\n",
    "                   c=cmap_bold[class_idx], label=f\"{class_name} (train)\",\n",
    "                   edgecolor=\"k\", s=45, alpha=0.8)\n",
    "        \n",
    "    ax.set_title(title, fontsize=13)\n",
    "    ax.set_xlabel(f\"Standardized {feat_names[0]}\")\n",
    "    ax.set_ylabel(f\"Standardized {feat_names[1]}\")\n",
    "    ax.legend(loc=\"upper left\", frameon=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 9: Decision Tree Structure Visualization\n",
    "Inspect the decision logic, threshold splits, and leaf node purity of the trained Decision Tree."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "plt.figure(figsize=(14, 8), dpi=120)\n",
    "plot_tree(\n",
    "    decision_tree,\n",
    "    feature_names=feature_cols,\n",
    "    class_names=labels,\n",
    "    filled=True,\n",
    "    rounded=True,\n",
    "    fontsize=11\n",
    ")\n",
    "plt.title(\"Trained Decision Tree (max_depth=3) Split Logic\", fontsize=15, pad=12)\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 10: Conclusion & Key Findings\n",
    "1. **Feature Separation:** The exploratory pairplot confirms that `petal_length` and `petal_width` provide clear linear separation for *Iris setosa*, while *Iris versicolor* and *Iris virginica* have slight boundary overlap.\n",
    "2. **Data Normalization:** `StandardScaler` scaled each feature to zero mean and unit variance without data leakage, stabilizing gradient convergence for `LogisticRegression`.\n",
    "3. **Model Performance:** Both `LogisticRegression` and `DecisionTreeClassifier` achieve high benchmark accuracy (~93% - 97%+) on the 80/20 test split.\n",
    "4. **Boundary Geometry:** The decision boundary visualization highlights that Logistic Regression partitions feature space with linear hyperplanes, whereas Decision Tree forms orthogonal, axis-parallel box partitions."
   ]
  }
 ],
